| RunStackFix - the fresh-stack problem, with the two fixes.  Installs nothing.  Output: ResultsStackFix in this directory.
|   A. readtest2-scp is readtest2 built with the compiler option -fstack-clash-protection: the compiler touches every page of a big local array when the function starts, in
|      user mode, so RISC OS never takes the page fault itself.  It must say "every byte right" with ANY libunixlib (16.2.0-1, -2 or -3).
|   B. readtest2 (built without it) is the same program as before: it says "every byte right" only with libunixlib 16.2.0-3 or later (which touches the pages itself).
| (the first EABI program run changes <Obey$Dir>, so remember our directory first)
Set RoTest$Dir <Obey$Dir>
Dir <RoTest$Dir>
Spool <RoTest$Dir>.ResultsStackFix
Echo ===================== which libunixlib is loaded (fix level 6 = 16.2.0-3 or later) and whether fread into a fresh stack buffer works
Run <RoTest$Dir>.ulinfo
Echo ===================== A. built with -fstack-clash-protection: read() and fread() into fresh stack buffers (every byte must be right)
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2-scp read 64
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2-scp read 512
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2-scp fread 64
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2-scp fread 512
Echo ===================== B. built normally (right only with libunixlib 16.2.0-3 or later)
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2 read 64
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2 read 512
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2 fread 64
Run <RoTest$Dir>.readtest2 fread 512
Spool
Echo Finished. Output is in <RoTest$Dir>.ResultsStackFix
